        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/GDQ-2026.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Some people get very excited for <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/everything-announced-in-summer-game-fest-2026\">our annual non-E3 blast of games news in June</a>. Others await the Q3-Q4 release window rush of games with glee (although, this year, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/gta-6-release-date-black-hole\">I find it a bit more scary than I do exciting</a>). My favourite time of the gaming calendar, though, is split between two six-month blocks: I celebrate the arrival of Summer Games Done Quick and Awesome Games Done Quick like the passing of Halley's Comet.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/summer-games-done-quick-2026-schedule\">Read more</a></p>",
